Now I have enough context. Let me implement the changes.

### 1) `assets/ca-data.js`: placeholder-team hygiene

Add:
```js
var SLOT_RE = /^слот\s*\d+$/i;
function isPlaceholderName(name) {
  var s = String(name == null ? '' : name).trim();
  if (!s) return true;
  if (SLOT_RE.test(s)) return true;
  if (/^команда\s*\d+$/i.test(s)) return true;
  return false;
}
function isRealTeam(t) { return !!t && !isPlaceholderName(t.name); }
```
Then in finalize:
- `D.champion = grand && grand.winner ? team(D, grand.winner) : null;` → after that, `if (D.champion && !isRealTeam(D.champion)) D.champion = null;` same for runnerUp.
- Also `D.hasRealTeams = D.teams.some(isRealTeam)`.
- Phase: `if (grand && grand.winner && D.champion) phase='post'` — hmm careful: if the champion team was deleted (id no longer exists), `team()` returns null → currently `D.phase='post'` still (because `grand.winner` is set). With the placeholder guard, `D.champion` null but winner set → phase post with no champion → weird states (home banner hidden, next-season block shows). Better: phase 'post' requires a *resolvable real* champion:
  `if (grand && grand.winner && D.champion) D.phase = 'post'`.
  If the winner id no longer resolves → the tournament isn't actually finished for display purposes; then if startFromServer && now >= start → 'live', else 'pre'. That's sane.

  Hmm, but there's a subtlety: if the org deletes the champion team after the final (bad idea), the site would flip back to 'live'. Acceptable.

- Also stats: `records` are built from matches; placeholder teams would appear in standings. Let me filter standings/records for placeholder teams: skip recording wins/losses for placeholder teams (or skip them from `standings`). Minimal: in `computeStats`, skip teams where `isPlaceholderName(t.name)` when creating records, and skip matches whose winner/loser are placeholders. That prevents "Слот 1 — 2 победы" in tables/club stats.

- Export `isPlaceholderName` and `hasRealTeams` on `CA.data`.

### 2) `assets/ca-history.js`: separation + robustness

Changes:
a) `allTime()`: guard `club(team)`: `if (!team || isSlotName(team.name)) return null;` and update callers to handle null (they already do `if (cw)`, `if (cc)`; need `if (cl)` checks — currently `cl.played++` after `if (l)`; make `club` return a dummy? Simpler: keep `club()` returning an object but guard at call sites with a helper `bumpClub(team, fn)`).

Let me restructure minimally:
```js
function club(team) {
  if (!team || isSlotName(team.name)) return null;
  ...
}
```
and at each call site: `var cw = club(w); if (cw) {...}` ✓ (already), `var cl = club(l); if (cl) {...}` (add), `var cc = club(champ); if (cc) { cc.titles++; cc.finals++; }` ✓, `club(runner)` → guard: `var cr = club(runner); if (cr) cr.finals++;`, `lc` similarly.

b) Season numbering & titles:
- `seasonTitle(item, index)` → disambiguated name: if another history item has the same `name`, append ` #N` (N = its chronological position). Simpler and clearer: always show the number in the chapter marker ("Турнир №1") and keep the raw name as the H2; plus if duplicate names exist → append " · " + date to the H2? Hmm, the date is already in the marker. Let me do: when duplicates exist among history names, H2 = `name + ' #' + n`. That reads "Compass Arena #1", "Compass Arena #2" ✓ exactly what the user wants ("точное разделение на 1 и 2 турнир").

Implementation: compute a map of name→count; then for each item assign `ordinal` (1-based chronological) and `label`:
```js
function decorateSeasons(sorted) {
  var counts = {}, seen = {};
  sorted.forEach(function (h) { var k = String(h.name||'Compass Arena').trim().toLowerCase(); counts[k] = (counts[k]||0)+1; });
  return sorted.map(function (h, i) {
    var k = ...;
    var ord = (seen[k] = (seen[k]||0)+1);
    var name = h.name || 'Compass Arena';
    var label = counts[k] > 1 ? name + ' #' + ord : name;
    return { h: h, index: i, ordinal: ord, label: label, season: i + 1 };
  });
}
```
Then pass `season` (i+1) and `label` into `chapterHtml`.

c) Chapter marker text: currently `Глава NN / MM`. Replace with an explicit season marker:
```
<div class="h-mark">
  <span class="no">Турнир №1 из 2</span>
  <span class="rule"></span>
  <span class="date">27.09.2030</span>
</div>
```
And for the current season: `Текущий сезон` → `Сезон №3 · регистрация` or `Сезон №3 · идёт`. Let me implement:
- current: `no` label = `'Сезон №' + (sorted.length+1)` and a status word: `' · регистрация'` / `' · идёт'` / `' · завершён'`. Chapter marker: `Сезон №3 · идёт` + dates.
- archive: `Турнир №N из M`.

This gives unambiguous separation.

d) Visual separation: add markup between chapters: `<div class="orn" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ic"><use href="#i-compass"></use></svg></div>` before each archive chapter; and alternate the section background via a class `is-alt` on odd/even chapters. Also add a "chapter index" section near the top (before chapters) listing all tournaments with number, date, champion — that's basically the champions table, which is at the bottom; I'll move/duplicate a compact index to the top of the archive (`#books`): "Хроника: 1 · Compass Arena #1 — 27.09.2030 — чемпион Team Spirit". Hmm, the `.h-nav` chips already do that. Let me instead make the nav chips carry the number + date: `№1 · Compass Arena #1 · 27.09.2030`. Keep chips reasonably short: `№1 · Compass Arena #1`. Good enough, and add the year.

Also: the champions table gets `№` ✓ (already) and the tournament anchor ✓, and I'll pass the disambiguated label into the table so it matches the chapters.

e) Robustness: wrap each chapter in try/catch:
```js
for (...) { try { archive += chapterHtml(...); } catch (e) { console.warn(...); archive += chapterFallback(item, i); } }
```
Also wrap `allTime`, `championsTable`, `clubsTable`, `mvpShowcase`, `currentHtml` in try/catch to guarantee the page never goes blank. And ensure `render()` is called inside a try/catch that at least writes the hero.

