content.text:
Now the big one: registration.js — full logic for the three branches.

Let me write it carefully.

```js
/* ============================================================
   Регистрация: команда / свободный агент / заявка игрока
   ...описание...
   ============================================================ */

import { sendMessage, editMessageText, answerCallbackQuery, inlineKeyboard, sendChatAction, notifyAdmins, getPhotoDataUrl } from '../lib/telegram.js';
import { getState, setState, resetState, createLead, canSubmitLead, findPendingTeamByName, getSetting } from '../lib/db.js';
import { esc, clean, isNick, isTeamName, plural } from '../lib/esc.js';
import { DISCIPLINE_KEYS, DISCIPLINES, disciplineLabel, roleByKey, roleLabel, roleNum, roleTitle, rolesOf } from '../lib/domain.js';

export const commands = ['skip'];               // /skip нужен на необязательных шагах
export const callbackPrefixes = ['reg'];
```

Steps constants (per ТЗ #6).

Screen functions returning {text, keyboard}.

Progress: `Шаг N из M`.

Let me define helper:
```js
const CANCEL_HINT = '\n\n<i>Отмена: /cancel</i>';
function textScreen(title, body, footer) → joined text
```

Screens:

1) `screenDiscipline(intro)`:
```
🏆 Compass Arena — регистрация
Выбери дисциплину:
```
keyboard: [🎯 Dota 2][🔫 CS:GO]
Actually start.js already has showMainMenu with the discipline keyboard; for reg:back at the very beginning I can call startHandler.showMainMenu — but that creates a circular import (registration imports start; start doesn't import registration ✓ no cycle). index.js imports both ✓. Let me import `showMainMenu` from './start.js' in registration.js — that's fine (no cycle since start.js doesn't import registration.js).

2) `screenType(discipline)`:
```
{emoji} <b>{label}</b>

Действие:
```
keyboard rows:
[🏆 Зарегистрировать команду] → reg:type:team
[🎯 Найти команду] → reg:type:looking
[🧍 Оставить заявку игрока] → reg:type:player
[⬅️ В меню] → act:menu

3) `screenTeamName(discipline)`:
```
{emoji} {label} · Заявка команды
<b>Шаг 1 из 7</b>

Как называется команда? (2–30 символов)
```
+ cancel hint. Keyboard: [⬅️ Назад] → reg:back  (back at team_name → show type screen)

4) `screenTeamLogo`: «Шаг 2 из 7» + «Пришли логотип команды фото или /skip».
keyboard: [⏭ Без логотипа] → reg:skip? Hmm — the ТЗ wants /skip for text; a button «Без логотипа» is a nice inline addition (and all buttons must be inline). Let me add [⏭ Пропустить] → `reg:logo:skip`. That doesn't conflict: ТЗ says "или /skip" — providing a button as well is extra convenience. Also [⬅️ Назад] → reg:back (back to name).

5) `screenPlayerNick(index)`:
```
<b>Шаг {3+index} из 7</b>
Ник игрока {index+1}?
```
+ cancel hint, keyboard: [⬅️ Назад] → reg:back (back: for player 0 → logo step; for others → previous player's role? On "back" from player N nick: return to the previous step: if index===0 → logo screen; else → role screen of player index-1? Simpler: back at nick → `reg:edit:player:index-1` (edit previous player's nick) for index>0, else logo screen. Hmm, "back" semantics: I'll implement `reg:back` to walk one step back in the current flow:
 - team_name → type screen
 - team_logo → team_name screen
 - player nick i → if i>0: player nick i-1 (allowing re-edit) else team_logo
 - player role i → player nick i
 - team_confirm → player role 4
 - edit_menu → team_confirm
 - agent_nick → type
 - agent_role → agent_nick
 - agent_rank → agent_role
 - agent_note → agent_rank
 - player_nick → type
 - player_team → player_nick
 - player_role → player_team
That's a coherent back navigation. I'll implement it as a function `goBack(ctx, state)`.

6) `screenPlayerRole(index, nick)`:
```
<b>Шаг {3+index} из 7</b>
Игрок {index+1}: <b>{nick}</b>
Выбери роль:
```
keyboard: role buttons in rows of 2 + Hmm, 5 buttons: dota2 → «1 — Керри», «2 — Мидер», ... (full titles, might be long: "4 — Саппорт 4" ~ 13 chars, fine). Layout: rows of 2+2+1 or 3+2. Let me do rows of 2,2,1:
[1 — Керри][2 — Мидер]
[3 — Офлейн][4 — Саппорт 4]
[5 — Саппорт 5]
For CS:GO: [IGL — Капитан][AWPer — Снайпер] / [Entry — Врывающийся][Support — Поддержка] / [Lurker — Луркер]
callback: reg:role:<key>
Plus [⬅️ Назад] → reg:back.

Careful: callback_data length — `reg:role:IGL` ✓ short.

7) `screenTeamConfirm(temp)`:
```
{emoji} {label} · <b>Шаг 7 из 7</b> · Проверка

Название: <b>{name}</b>
Логотип: ✅ загружен (45 КБ){ / ⚠️ принят как есть, больше 200 КБ}{ / — не загружен}

1. Yatoro — Керри
...
```
keyboard: [✅ Подтвердить][✏️ Изменить] and [⬅️ Назад]
callback: reg:confirm / reg:edit / reg:back

8) `screenEditMenu(temp)`:
```
✏️ Что изменить?
Название: Team Spirit
Логотип: ✅
1. Yatoro — Керри
...
```
keyboard: [✏️ Название][✏️ Логотип] [✏️ Игрок 1..5 (по 2 в ряд)] [◀ Назад]
callbacks: reg:edit:name, reg:edit:logo, reg:edit:player:N, reg:back

9) Branch B screens: agent_nick (Шаг 1 из 4 — «Твой ник?»), agent_role (Шаг 2 из 4 — «Твоя позиция?»), agent_rank (Шаг 3 из 4 — «Твой ранг? (или /skip)»), agent_note (Шаг 4 из 4 — «Пара слов о себе? (или /skip)»).
Note: branch B has no confirmation screen in the ТЗ → after note → submit immediately.

10) Branch C: player_nick (1/3), player_team (2/3 — «В какой команде играешь? (или /skip)»), player_role (3/3 — «Твоя позиция?») → submit.

Now the handlers.

```js
export async function handleCommand(env, message, ctx) {
  if (ctx.cmd !== 'skip') return false;
  return await handleSkip(env, ctx);
}
```

handleSkip:
```js
const state = await getState(env, ctx.userId);
if (!state.step) { await sendMessage(..., 'Сейчас нечего пропускать. /start — начать регистрацию.'); return true; }
switch (state.step) {
  case 'team_logo': case 'team_edit_field' (editField logo) → set logo '' → continue
  case 'agent_rank' → rank '' → next
  case 'agent_note' → note '' → submit
  case 'player_team' → teamName null → next
  default: await sendMessage(env, ctx.chatId, 'Здесь /skip не нужен — выполни текущий шаг или нажми /cancel.'); return true;
}
```

Now the flow functions. Let me define a generic "advance" pattern:

```js
async function send(env, ctx, screen) {  // screen = {text, keyboard}
  await sendMessage(env, ctx.chatId, screen.text, { keyboard: screen.keyboard });
}
async function replace(env, ctx, screen) {  // для кнопочной навигации: правим то же сообщение
  if (ctx.messageId) {
    try { await editMessageText(env, ctx.chatId, ctx.messageId, screen.text, { keyboard: screen.keyboard }); return; }
    catch (err) { console.warn('[reg] не удалось отредактировать сообщение:', err.message); }
  }
  await send(env, ctx, screen);
}
```
For text-input steps we always `send` a new message. For button navigation we `replace`.

But there's a subtlety: when we're at a text-input step and it *completes*, the next screen may be a button screen; using `send` is fine.

However, when a text step completes and we show the NEXT text step, we send a new message ✓.

For the confirm screen after the last role button: `replace` (edits the role message) ✓.

State transitions helpers:
```js
async function setStep(env, userId, step, temp) { await setState(env, userId, step, temp); }
```

Let me write the team flow:

```js
async function startTeam(env, ctx, state, discipline) {
  const temp = { ...state.temp, discipline, type: 'team', name: '', logo: '', logoOversized: false, players: [], playerIndex: 0, editField: null };
  await setState(env, ctx.userId, STEP.TEAM_NAME, temp);
  await replace(env, ctx, screenTeamName(discipline));
}
```

onTeamName(env, ctx, state, raw):
```js
const name = clean(raw);
if (!isTeamName(name)) {
  await send(env, ctx, { text: `⚠️ Название от 2 до 30 символов, буквы и цифры.\n\n<b>Шаг 1 из 7</b>\nНазвание команды?` + CANCEL, keyboard: backKeyboard });
  return true;   // шаг не меняем
}
const temp = { ...state.temp, name };
await setState(env, ctx.userId, STEP.TEAM_LOGO, temp);
await send(env, ctx, screenTeamLogo(temp, `✅ Название: <b>${esc(name)}</b>`));
```
Hmm, the ТЗ error text: «Название от 2 до 30 символов, буквы и цифры.» ✓ use it. Prefix with ⚠️ — fine (ТЗ says «Отказ: ...»).

For logo:
```js
async function onLogoText(env, ctx, state, raw) {
  if (/^\/?skip$/i.test(clean(raw))) → no logo
  else → hint: 'Пришли логотип фотографией или нажми /skip.'
}
async function onLogoPhoto(env, message, ctx) {
  const state = await getState(env, ctx.userId);
  if (!(state.step === STEP.TEAM_LOGO || (state.step === STEP.TEAM_EDIT_FIELD && state.temp.editField === 'logo'))) return false;
