Good progress: 124 passed, 5 failed. The debug hint shows state = "team_confirm" — so the flow DID complete, and the "нужно нажать кнопку" text wasn't found. Let me think why.

In `handleText`:
```js
export async function handleText(env, message, ctx) {
  const state = await getState(env, ctx.userId);
  if (!state.step) return false;
  ...
  switch (state.step) {
    case STEP.TEAM_NAME: ...
    ...
    default:
      await sendMessage(env, ctx.chatId, 'На этом шаге нужно нажать кнопку ниже или отменить всё командой /cancel.', ...);
      return true;
  }
}
```
State = 'team_confirm' → not in the switch cases → default → sends the hint ✓. So `textsSince(mark)` should contain it...

Unless `handleText` is never called because an EARLIER handler's `handleText` returned true! index.js iterates HANDLERS in order: [start, registration, moderation, export]. start's handleText matches `/^(меню|начать|start|menu|привет|здравствуйте|hi|hello)$/i` — 'привет' MATCHES! So start.js handles it: resetState + showMainMenu → state becomes null ✗✗ That's exactly the bug my test caught: typing "привет" mid-flow wipes the progress.

That's a real UX bug: greeting words reset the registration. Fix: start.js's handleText should only react to menu words when there's NO active step. Let me implement: in start.js's handleText, check the state first:
```js
export async function handleText(env, message, ctx) {
  if (!/^(меню|начать|start|menu|привет|здравствуйте|hi|hello)$/i.test(ctx.text)) return false;
  const state = await getState(env, ctx.userId);
  if (state.step) {
    // идёт диалог — не сбрасываем его, подсказываем как выйти
    await sendMessage(env, ctx.chatId, 'Ты в середине регистрации. Продолжи текущий шаг или нажми /cancel.', { keyboard: inlineKeyboard([[{text:'🏠 В меню', data:'act:menu'}]]) });
    return true;
  }
  await showMainMenu(env, ctx.chatId, ctx.userId);
  return true;
}
```
That keeps the "привет → menu" behavior outside flows and protects flows ✓. And my test asserting "нужно нажать кнопку" would then get the start.js message instead → I should adjust the test: expect either the registration hint or the start.js hint, both meaning "прогресс не потерян". Let me assert on state preservation + a hint that mentions /cancel. Better: make the test message a neutral word that isn't a greeting, e.g. 'что-то' → then registration's default branch handles it ✓ and the assertion holds. And add a SEPARATE test that a greeting mid-flow doesn't wipe the state (valuable regression test).

Let me do both: fix start.js (protect flows) + test with a neutral word + add a greeting test.

Now the other failures:

1. **"в карточке весь состав с ролями"** — `/1\. <b>Yatoro<\/b> — Керри/`. The card text renders `playersList(temp)` → `${index + 1}. <b>${esc(player.nick)}</b>${role}` where role = ` — ${esc(player.roleLabel)}` ✓ → "1. <b>Yatoro</b> — Керри" ✓ should match... unless the card shown is from the *last* edit (registerTeam ends with role:5 → TEAM_CONFIRM) ✓. Hmm, but `lastTo(USER)` — the last message to USER. After the confirm card, is there another message to USER? No (notifyAdmins goes to ADMIN) ✓. 

Wait — maybe the card text uses `esc(player.roleLabel)` where roleLabel is 'Керри' ✓. Let me print the card text in the failure message to see. Also `/Miposhka — Саппорт 5/` — hmm, `playersList` uses `player.roleLabel` = 'Саппорт 5' ✓.

Hmm, maybe the issue: `teamCard` is called with `temp` — and in `onRole` after the 5th player I call `setState(...TEAM_CONFIRM, updated)` then `replace(screenTeamConfirm(updated, '✅ Состав собран...'))`. `replace` uses editMessageText with the ROLE message → the role screen was sent as a NEW message (send) and its id = ctx.messageId from the callback ✓ (the role buttons are on that message) ✓ so edit works — BUT my mock's `editMessageText` handler returns `{message_id: calls.length}` ✓ fine.

So why no match? Let me debug by printing the actual card text. Let me add the text as the `extra` argument on failure.

2. **"устаревшая кнопка роли не ломает сценарий"** and **"/skip на неподходящем шаге"** — these failed likely as a consequence of the earlier state reset (by 'привет') — since the state was wiped by start.js, the subsequent tests operated on a null state ✓ that explains both. After fixing the greeting issue they should pass, though the role-button test expects `/устарела|начни заново/` in texts OR answers: at that point (state=team_confirm) pressing reg:role:2 → onRole → state.step is TEAM_CONFIRM → `isTeamRole` false, etc. → answerCallbackQuery with 'Кнопка устарела — начни заново: /start' ✓ and my check looks at `textsSince(mark) + answers().map(a => a.body.text)` — `answers()` collects ALL answers (including earlier ones) ✓ fine. But `answerCallbackQuery` in telegram.js has showAlert — the text is in `body.text` ✓.

Hmm, careful: `answers()` returns all calls with method answerCallbackQuery across the whole test file? No — `calls` is reset by each `mockTelegram()` call; in block 9 the mock was called once at the top ✓ so answers() has the current block's answers ✓.

So after fixing the greeting bug, both should pass.

Let me now:
a) Fix start.js handleText (protect active flows).
b) Change the test's neutral word to 'что-то' and add a greeting-mid-flow test.
c) Debug the card assertion by adding the actual text to the failure output.

Let me look at the card text by adding `lastTo(USER)` as extra in the assertion, then run to see what it actually contains.

